{"TELL_NAME","reg=club|st=neutral,careful",{"Noted, you don't mean anything to me yet","We'll see if it means anything"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=club|st=friendly",{"Nice to meet you, don't cause trouble and we're good"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=crime|st=neutral,careful",{"Noted, I have a good memory, in case you were wondering","I'll check it against what I hear"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=crime|st=friendly",{"Pleasure, I make a point of remembering friendly names"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=prison|st=neutral,careful",{"That's-- fine, whatever, I'm staying over here","Don't, uh, don't come any closer, alright?"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=prison|st=friendly",{"Hey, good to meet you, been a while since somebody said their name to me"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=outlaw|st=neutral,careful",{"Uh-huh, and I'm supposed to trust that","Doesn't mean much out here but alright"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=outlaw|st=friendly",{"Good to meet you, folks I can put a name to I can trust a little"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=law|st=neutral,careful",{"Thank you, I'll note it, please keep your hands where I can see them","Understood, stay calm and we'll sort this out"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=law|st=hostile",{"That checks out? We'll see, don't move"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=law|st=friendly",{"Good to meet you, take a breath, you're among decent people"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=swat|st=neutral,careful",{"Copy, noted, stand by"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=military|st=neutral,careful",{"Copy that, I'll make a note of it","Understood, stay where you are"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=military|st=friendly",{"Nice to meet you, we'll try to help if we can"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=elite|st=neutral,careful",{"Noted, and I do not forget names"}},
{"TELL_NAME","role=militia|st=neutral,careful",{"Fine, welcome to the township, keep the peace and we'll keep ours"}},
{"TELL_NAME","role=militia|st=friendly",{"Pleased to meet you, any friend of the neighborhood is a friend of mine"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=civilian,family,worker,rescue|tmp=fresh|st=friendly,neutral",{"Nice to meet you... I'm awful with names, I'll forget it, sorry","That's a good name, strong, I wish I had a strong name","Hi, hi, I hope we can be friends, I'm sorry, that's weird"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=civilian,family,worker,rescue|tmp=seasoned|st=friendly,neutral",{"Good to know, I'll try to remember it, no promises","Nice to meet you, I'd shake your hand, but you know, germs","Friend, I've got it, I'll be saying it a lot"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=civilian,family,worker,rescue|tmp=seasoned|st=careful,neutral",{"I'll remember it, as long as you remember mine"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=family|st=friendly,neutral",{"What a lovely name, dear, your mother must have been proud"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=law,swat|st=friendly,neutral",{"Noted, I'll add it to the log"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=military,elite|st=friendly,neutral",{"Understood, name logged"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=outlaw,raider,gang,club,crime,prison|st=friendly,neutral",{"Ha, a real name? Cute, I'll call you Pal"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=civilian,family,worker,rescue|st=neutral,careful,hostile|rep=worst",{"Oh- no, no, that name, that's the name they... oh God, please","That's you? THAT'S you? okay, okay, breathe, everything's fine, nobody's moving","Funny, I'd heard that name, in a nightmare I thought, okay..."}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=civilian,family,worker,rescue|st=careful,neutral|rep=bad",{"I know that name, mm, we'll keep it short, then","So that's the name that goes with the stories, hm, fine, I'm listening but I'm watching too","That's a name I've heard in bad company, prove me wrong","Alright, I've heard about that name, not much good, don't prove it right"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=civilian,family,worker,rescue|st=friendly,neutral|rep=good",{"That's you? Oh wow, they told me about you, they said you were decent! nice to meet you!","Oh, I know that name! good things, mostly... sorry, mostly... all good things","Wait, THE one? from the stories? okay, okay, I feel better already","That name's got a good ring round here, good to put a face on it"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=civilian,family,worker,rescue|st=friendly,neutral|rep=best",{"No way, no WAY, you're real, my brother swore somebody made you up","You're- you're THE Legend?! Listen to me, I'm gushing, God","Everybody's heard that name, everybody, I never thought I'd hear it said out loud"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=law,swat|st=careful,neutral|rep=bad",{"That name's in my notes, under things I'd like to stop reading about","I know that name, not fondly, just so you know"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=law,swat|st=friendly,neutral|rep=good",{"That's your name? Good, I've had it in my notes under 'people who help'","Ah, I know that name, folks at the station speak well of it"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=military,elite|st=careful,neutral|rep=bad",{"Name noted, reputation noted, proceed with caution","That name is flagged on my side, I'm not saying more"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=military,elite|st=friendly,neutral|rep=good",{"Good, I know that name, higher-ups will want to hear we met, in a nice way"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=outlaw,raider,gang,club,crime,prison|st=neutral,careful,hostile|rep=worst",{"Hah! THAT name! you're the one who... hell, I need to sit down","So it IS you, pleasure, honest, please keep it that way"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=outlaw,raider,gang,club,crime,prison|st=careful,neutral|rep=bad",{"Yeah, I know it, nice and ugly, I like it, don't get cocky"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=outlaw,raider,gang,club,crime,prison|st=friendly,neutral|rep=good",{"Hm, that name rings a bell, wasn't a bad bell, not a good one for us though"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=civilian,family|tmp=fresh|st=friendly,neutral",{"Nice to meet you - really, I'm trying to remember everybody's name now - it seems important"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=civilian,family|tmp=fresh|st=friendly",{"Okay, I'm gonna say it in my head a couple of times so I don't forget - there"}},
{"TELL_NAME","role=family_woman|st=friendly,neutral",{"Pleased to meet you, hon, I'd offer you sweet tea if there was any ice left in the world"}},
{"TELL_NAME","role=family_elder|st=friendly,neutral",{"Good name, strong - your mama picked well"}},
{"TELL_NAME","role=family_youth|st=friendly,neutral",{"Cool, I'm bad with names, so if I call you 'hey' later, that's why"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=civilian,family,worker|tmp=seasoned,veteran|st=friendly,neutral",{"Alright, now there's a name to go with the face, that's rarer than it used to be","Good to know, if I find you face down somewhere, I'll know what to carve on the cross"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=worker|st=friendly,neutral",{"Got it, now I know who to holler for when I need a hand with the heavy end"}},
{"TELL_NAME","role=rescue_medical|st=friendly,neutral",{"Thank you, I write down everyone I see - just in case somebody comes looking for them"}},
{"TELL_NAME","role=rescue_clergy|st=friendly,neutral|hour=16,5",{"I'll remember you in my prayers tonight - by name, that matters more than people think"}},
{"TELL_NAME","role=rescue_firefighter|st=friendly,neutral",{"Good, if you go down near me, that's what I'll be shouting"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=civilian,family,worker,rescue|st=hostile",{"I don't care what you're called, I care where your feet are, and they're on my land"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=law|st=friendly,neutral",{"Appreciate that, if folks come asking, I'll know you passed through here"}},
{"TELL_NAME","role=law_trooper,law_officer|st=friendly,neutral",{"Thank you - got any ID on you? No? Didn't figure - just habit"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=law,swat|st=careful",{"Okay, I'd run that through dispatch, but there's no dispatch - stay put anyway"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=law,swat|st=hostile",{"I don't care what your name is, face down on the ground"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=swat|st=friendly,neutral",{"Good to know your name"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=military|tmp=seasoned,veteran|st=friendly,neutral",{"All right. I'll try to remember it"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=military|tmp=fresh|st=friendly,neutral,careful",{"Okay! Nice to meet you, I'm, oh, I'm not supposed to give mine - sorry"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=military|st=careful,hostile",{"Your name doesn't change where you're standing - back up"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=elite|st=friendly,neutral",{"Logged"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=elite|st=careful,hostile",{"Didn't ask for it"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=outlaw|st=friendly,neutral|hour=16,22",{"Pleased to meet you, I'll forget it by sundown, no offense - safer for both of us"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=outlaw|st=careful,hostile",{"You won't get mine, call it rude if you want"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=raider|st=friendly,neutral",{"Nice, now I know what to yell when I want your stuff"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=gang|st=friendly,neutral|world=building",{"Cool name - be a shame if somebody had to spray it on a wall"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=club|st=friendly,neutral",{"That's a square's name, we'd have to give you a real one if you stuck around"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=prison|st=friendly,neutral",{"Heh, same as a fella I did county time with, he talked to the guards - you a talker?"},false,{[1]="GENERIC"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=raider,gang,club,prison|st=careful",{"Don't matter to me, you're still standing too close"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=raider,gang,club,prison|st=hostile",{"Don't care, I'll just call you Dead Weight"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=crime|st=friendly,neutral",{"A name is a kind of collateral, thank you for the deposit"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=crime|st=careful,hostile",{"Now we know who you are, you still don't know who we are - think about that"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=civilian|tmp=fresh|st=friendly,neutral",{"Okay, I'll try to hang onto it, I've been bad at names since the fourth"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=family|st=friendly",{"Good to know you, we had a Ray in this family, he was the loud one"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=worker|tmp=seasoned|st=friendly,neutral|world=door",{"Alright, I'll write it on the door frame with the rest of 'em"}},
{"TELL_NAME","role=rescue_clergy|st=friendly",{"I'll put you on the list, that's all the list is - names of folks still here"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=law|st=neutral",{"Spell the last one for me, I'm writing it down whether you like it or not"}},
{"TELL_NAME","role=soldier_nco|tmp=veteran|st=neutral",{"Okay, I'll use it after we've been somewhere unpleasant together"}},
{"TELL_NAME","role=rescue_medical|st=friendly|mood=warm",{"Say it once more, I want to say it back so it sticks"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=civilian|tmp=seasoned|st=friendly",{"Huh, first name I've learned in nine days, I'll keep hold of it"}},
{"TELL_NAME","reg=raider,outlaw|tmp=predator|st=hostile",{"A name - how nice, names are for folks who plan on being remembered"}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=family_man|st=neutral,friendly",{"When our first kid was on the way, I offered to paper the little bedroom myself"},false,false,{[1]={{t="My wife picked a pattern with ducks on it, and I got most of one wall done before she came to look",afterMs=2600},{t="She stood there a while before she asked whether ducks usually swam upside down. I'd been matching the wrong ends",afterMs=2800},{t="We put the crib in front of the worst bit. She'd point out my wall whenever somebody said the baby looked like me",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=family_woman|st=neutral,careful,friendly",{"My father taught me to drive in his pickup, out where there wasn't much to run into"},false,false,{[1]={{t="Every time I stalled it, he'd reach for the dashboard like that would help, and it made me madder than anything he said",afterMs=2600},{t="Finally I told him to get out. He did, and stood by the fence while I tried again",afterMs=2800},{t="When I got it moving, I went straight past him, clear to the next gate. He had a good long walk before I let him back in",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=family_elder|st=neutral,friendly",{"At a reunion in West Point I insisted on a proper family photograph, with everybody standing still"},false,false,{[1]={{t="I spent so long straightening collars that the little ones sat down in the grass, and my brother sat with them",afterMs=2600},{t="The photographer went ahead without me. In the picture I'm off to one side with a comb in my mouth",afterMs=2800},{t="My sister ordered that one, not the one I finally lined up. Gave me the biggest copy she could get",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=family_youth|st=neutral,friendly",{"We got ten minutes at a school talent show and spent two weeks arguing over what to call the band"},false,false,{[1]={{t="On the night, the drummer's dad brought the kit in his truck but left the stool in their kitchen",afterMs=2600},{t="We borrowed a chair with a bent leg, so he had to brace it with one foot through the whole song. We only knew one song anyway",afterMs=2800},{t="He wanted to quit afterward. Mostly he wanted someone to ask why nobody had helped him carry anything",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=civilian_man|st=neutral,careful,friendly",{"I tried growing tomatoes one summer, right beside the steps of the place I rented"},false,false,{[1]={{t="I read the directions twice. Still planted them where the roof kept the rain off",afterMs=2600},{t="The woman next door finally came over with a watering can and asked whether I was trying to dry them on the vine",afterMs=2800},{t="After that she checked them whenever she checked her own. I got four tomatoes and gave her the two that weren't split",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=civilian_woman|st=friendly",{"I wore the heel off one good shoe and took it to a little repair place in Louisville"},false,false,{[1]={{t="The man said he'd fix both, otherwise I'd walk crooked, and I argued because I'd only brought enough cash for one",afterMs=2600},{t="He waved me out and told me to bring the rest Friday. It was nearly a month before I went back",afterMs=2800},{t="He didn't mention the money until I did. Asked whether the shoes had quit hurting first",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=civilian_loner|st=friendly",{"Lived next to a man for four years and never learned his name until his gas bill landed in my mailbox"},false,false,{[1]={{t="I walked it over and said the name wrong, so he thought I was there to sell him something",afterMs=2600},{t="We had a whole argument through the screen before I could show him the envelope. Then he asked if I wanted coffee",afterMs=2800},{t="I said no, automatically. Went back the next morning and knocked before I'd thought of a reason",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=worker|st=neutral,careful,friendly",{"First week at a cabinet shop, they had me sweep while the older men worked"},false,false,{[1]={{t="I swept up a little pencil stub with the shavings and got a louder dressing-down than I'd had for being late",afterMs=2600},{t="The man had sharpened that thing down until it hardly stuck out of his fist. There were new pencils in a drawer, but he wanted that one",afterMs=2800},{t="I found it under the bench after everybody left. Set it by his cup next morning, and neither of us said anything",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=rescue_firefighter|st=neutral,careful,friendly",{"We went to a chimney fire once and the woman at the door kept pointing at our boots"},false,false,{[1]={{t="She'd just had pale carpet put down, and she wanted us to go round to the kitchen entrance",afterMs=2600},{t="After it was out, she brought a kettle to the truck and apologized so much I couldn't get a word in",afterMs=2800},{t="I went back past that house a week later. There was a stack of old towels by the front door",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=rescue_medical|st=neutral,friendly",{"On a late ambulance run, a man kept asking whether we'd left his porch light on"},false,false,{[1]={{t="I told him we hadn't touched it, but he asked again every few minutes, so I started wondering if I'd missed something",afterMs=2600},{t="Turned out his daughter was driving in from Lexington and had never seen the house. That light was how he'd told her to find it",afterMs=2800},{t="We got someone to call her at home before she left. I remember him asking if she'd sounded annoyed",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=rescue_clergy|st=neutral,careful,friendly",{"A pipe burst at the church one winter, and we had Sunday service in the high-school cafeteria"},false,false,{[1]={{t="I stood under the menu board trying to get through a funeral announcement, with Tuesday Tacos over my head",afterMs=2600},{t="A boy started laughing and his mother dragged him out. I wanted to call them back, but I couldn't look at that sign without laughing either",afterMs=2800},{t="We moved the lectern after that. The boy helped, very solemn, like we'd both been caught",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=law_deputy|st=neutral,careful,friendly",{"One of my first summonses went to a cousin who used to take me fishing"},false,false,{[1]={{t="He opened the door and called me Deputy, real formal, before I'd even got the paper out",afterMs=2600},{t="I gave him the whole explanation I'd practiced. Then he asked if I was still coming over to help move his freezer",afterMs=2800},{t="I said yes, sir. He shut the door laughing, and I had to knock again because I'd forgotten to hand him the summons",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=law_sheriff|st=neutral,careful,friendly",{"During my first campaign for sheriff, my sister volunteered to paint signs, which ought to have warned me"},false,false,{[1]={{t="She used the leftover pink from her bathroom because she didn't see a reason to buy more",afterMs=2600},{t="I put one up at the feed store and a man asked if I was running for something or announcing a baby. Had to stand there while he finished laughing",afterMs=2800},{t="My sister made me return every sign after the election. She wanted the boards for her garden",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=law_officer|st=friendly",{"A man locked his keys in his car outside the courthouse, and I stayed with him while his brother fetched the spare"},false,false,{[1]={{t="He was wearing a suit in that heat, and I made some joke about being dressed for trouble",afterMs=2600},{t="Said he'd just come from signing divorce papers. I apologized, but he kept telling me it was a good suit",afterMs=2800},{t="When his brother arrived, he took the tie off and folded it very carefully before he got in",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=law_sergeant|st=neutral,careful,friendly",{"A retiring officer left me a cigar box full of keys, all carefully numbered"},false,false,{[1]={{t="I asked for the list that went with them and he said he'd kept it in his head for twenty-six years",afterMs=2600},{t="We spent his last afternoon trying doors instead of having the cake. Some numbers didn't fit anything in that building",afterMs=2800},{t="He called two weeks later to ask for number fourteen. It opened his sister's shed",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=law_trooper|st=neutral,careful,friendly",{"I stopped a family on their way to a campground because their trunk wasn't latched"},false,false,{[1]={{t="The father got out already arguing about his speed, while his wife kept trying to tell him why I'd stopped them",afterMs=2600},{t="He finally saw a quilt hanging out and went quiet. His little boy asked if I'd arrested the quilt",afterMs=2800},{t="The mother laughed so hard she had to lean on the car. The father wouldn't look at either of us",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=law_corrections|st=neutral,friendly",{"We had a mystery paperback on the book cart with the last ten pages torn out"},false,false,{[1]={{t="Men kept passing it back because they wanted the ending, and the librarian couldn't find another copy",afterMs=2600},{t="One of the older inmates wrote an ending in pencil on the blank pages. Wasn't much of a mystery after he put himself in it",afterMs=2800},{t="They argued about his version for days. Somebody asked me to check it back in under his name",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=swat_lead|st=friendly",{"At a Christmas party I got talked into playing Santa because nobody else would fit the coat"},false,false,{[1]={{t="A little girl told me her mother needed a washing machine, and I sat there with a bag of candy canes like an idiot",afterMs=2600},{t="I asked what she wanted for herself. She said her mother had to wash everything in the sink",afterMs=2800},{t="One of the women running the party came over and took the girl to find her mother. I was glad to let her do the talking",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=swat_operator|st=neutral,friendly",{"I spent a Saturday in a dunk tank to help raise money for a school roof"},false,false,{[1]={{t="They gave me a mouthful of insults to yell, but the first person in line was the woman who'd taught me fifth grade",afterMs=2600},{t="I called her ma'am and asked how she'd been. She hit the target before I'd finished",afterMs=2800},{t="The water was cold enough that I came up swearing. She told me she hoped I didn't talk like that at work",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=soldier|st=neutral,friendly",{"My brother sent me a model airplane he'd built, wrapped in a whole Sunday newspaper"},false,false,{[1]={{t="Both wings came off in the mail, so I spent a free afternoon trying to glue it back before I wrote him",afterMs=2600},{t="A man down the hall came over with tweezers and made me leave it alone while he worked. Had built models with his own boy",afterMs=2800},{t="He put one wing on crooked and got more upset than I did. We left it that way when the glue dried",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=soldier_nco|st=neutral,careful,friendly",{"A young private asked me to help with his tie before he went to meet his girlfriend's parents"},false,false,{[1]={{t="I could inspect one, but tying the damn things had always been my wife's job. Didn't tell him that",afterMs=2600},{t="We shut the door and worked at it until he was late. He had the same anxious look every time I undid it",afterMs=2800},{t="In the end he wore an open collar. Came back and told me her father hadn't worn a tie either",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=soldier_green|st=friendly",{"There was a girl in my class I meant to ask to the prom, and I kept waiting until I could catch her alone"},false,false,{[1]={{t="A friend finally asked her for me without telling me he was going to. Came back and said she'd said yes",afterMs=2600},{t="I thought he was kidding, so I never called her. Found out after the dance she'd waited half the evening",afterMs=2800},{t="When I tried to apologize, she asked why I'd believed him about everything except that. I didn't have much to say",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=deserter|st=friendly",{"My sister asked me to come to her graduation, and I told her I'd see about getting leave"},false,false,{[1]={{t="I had the leave. Spent it with some friends instead, figuring she'd be too busy to notice who wasn't there",afterMs=2600},{t="She mailed a photograph afterward and wrote that the ceremony had been boring anyway",afterMs=2800},{t="I started a letter about it twice. Both times I got stuck trying to make my excuse sound less stupid",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=militia|st=neutral,careful,friendly",{"I used to mark the lines for the little-league field on Saturday mornings"},false,false,{[1]={{t="One summer I got into a bitter argument with another father about where home plate ought to be",afterMs=2600},{t="We measured it twice and were still at it when the kids came out. They took their ball over behind the bleachers and started without us",afterMs=2800},{t="We left the plate where it was. Stood at the fence and argued about whose turn it was to umpire",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=elite_operator|st=friendly",{"I got roped into a card game at an aunt's house and spent the first hour trying to work out who was cheating"},false,false,{[1]={{t="One woman kept leaning over her husband's cards and whispering to him, loudly enough that I figured everybody knew",afterMs=2600},{t="I finally said something. My aunt told me his eyesight had gone and he couldn't read his own hand",afterMs=2800},{t="Then she reached under the table and took a card off him herself. I never did work out the rules they were using",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=elite_delta|st=neutral,friendly",{"An elevator stopped between floors while I was in it with a man carrying flowers"},false,false,{[1]={{t="He was sweating through his shirt and kept checking his watch, so I told him nobody would blame him for being late",afterMs=2600},{t="He said the flowers were for his wife, not a delivery. It was their first anniversary, and he'd already been late for the wedding",afterMs=2800},{t="We were in there long enough that he pulled out the card and rewrote it. Never saw what he put",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=outlaw|st=neutral,careful,friendly",{"Borrowed a jon boat to take a woman fishing, and spent the whole morning pretending I'd used it before"},false,false,{[1]={{t="The motor wouldn't start, and every time I leaned over it she asked if she should hold my feet",afterMs=2600},{t="We finally tied up close enough to shore that she could step out and go buy sandwiches. I caught one little bluegill while she was gone",afterMs=2800},{t="She asked me out again. Said she'd arrange the boat next time",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=raider|st=neutral,careful,friendly",{"A man I knew paid me to feed his lizard while he was out of town, and I took the money before I saw it"},false,false,{[1]={{t="Big damn thing, stretched across a branch in a glass tank. Turned its head every time I moved",afterMs=2600},{t="I got my little cousin to come over, told him I was letting him help. He reached straight in while I stood by the door",afterMs=2800},{t="He made me hand over half the money before he'd come back the next day. Wouldn't take my word for it",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=raider_boss|st=friendly",{"My mother made me cut my little brother's hair because I'd been bragging I could do it"},false,false,{[1]={{t="He kept ducking away, so I held his head still and told him to quit whining. Made a bare stripe right above his ear",afterMs=2600},{t="Tried to even it up, which made it worse. By the time she came back, he had a towel over his head and wouldn't speak to me",afterMs=2800},{t="She took him to a barber and made me pay. He sat in the front seat on the way home, though I was older",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=gang_member|st=neutral,friendly",{"I spent a whole Saturday trying to tape a song off the radio for a girl who'd asked me for it"},false,false,{[1]={{t="Missed the start twice, and the disc jockey talked over the ending when I finally got it",afterMs=2600},{t="My brother had the record all along. Watched me keep restarting the tape and didn't say a damn thing until supper",afterMs=2800},{t="I made him record it for me after that. Left his voice saying to push the other button right before the song",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=gang_boss|st=neutral,careful,friendly",{"My uncle moved into an upstairs apartment and got me and another man to carry his sofa"},false,false,{[1]={{t="He kept telling us which way to turn it from the landing, where he wasn't carrying anything",afterMs=2600},{t="We wedged it so tight a woman upstairs couldn't get past. She stood there with a bag of frozen peas going soft while we argued",afterMs=2800},{t="We got it loose by taking it back down. Told him he could sleep on it there if he was that attached",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=biker|st=neutral,friendly",{"My nephew asked me to fix his bicycle the afternoon before his birthday"},false,false,{[1]={{t="I spread the parts on his mother's good table, then had to move the whole mess when she brought the cake in",afterMs=2600},{t="He kept asking when he'd get it back. I kept telling him soon, until the party was over and he'd gone to bed",afterMs=2800},{t="I finished it when everybody else was asleep and left it by his door. His mother made me come back the next day to clean the table",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=biker_boss|st=friendly",{"I accused a man of skimming twenty dollars from the club's dues, in front of everybody"},false,false,{[1]={{t="He emptied his pockets onto the table and told me to count it myself. There wasn't enough there to pay for his supper",afterMs=2600},{t="Two days later I found the missing bill folded into the receipt book. I'd put it there",afterMs=2800},{t="I apologized at the next meeting. He asked me to say it louder, so I did",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=crime_member|st=neutral,friendly",{"I took my little brother to an expensive restaurant in Lexington and ordered something I couldn't pronounce"},false,false,{[1]={{t="I pointed at the menu like I knew exactly what it was. He asked me straight out, and I told him I'd had it before",afterMs=2600},{t="The waiter brought out snails. My brother started laughing, and I got so angry I asked for the check before we'd eaten",afterMs=2800},{t="He made the waiter leave the plates. Ate his and half of mine while I sat there, then asked if we were still going to the movies",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=prisoner|st=friendly",{"When the guards stopped coming round, a man on my tier kept straightening his bunk for inspection"},false,false,{[1]={{t="People yelled at him to stop fussing and come with them, but he wanted the corners pulled tight",afterMs=2600},{t="I was near the door already. He asked if I'd give him a hand with the mattress, and I told him there wasn't time",afterMs=2800},{t="Then I went back and helped, angry the whole minute it took. He walked out ahead of me without looking at the bed",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=mercenary|st=neutral,friendly",{"Before anybody paid me to carry a rifle, I got a night job watching a piano showroom"},false,false,{[1]={{t="I couldn't play, but there was one upright by the window with a note taped over a broken key",afterMs=2600},{t="Spent most of a week trying to pick out a tune without touching that note. On Friday the owner came in early and stood listening",afterMs=2800},{t="He asked if I'd like lessons instead of more hours. I needed the hours, so I said no before he could tell me what they'd cost",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=raider|st=neutral,careful",{"I bought a bowling trophy at a yard sale outside Radcliff. Quarter, maybe fifty cents","A story? Fine, why not... first person I ever robbed was a preacher","Got a story for you, free of charge... I was a nobody, worked a loading dock in Louisville","You want a story? I had a dog once, big old mutt, named him Ranger","Story? Okay, okay... I stole a jukebox once, a whole damn jukebox, from a bar in Radcliff","Heh... you really wanna hear? Last winter I robbed a guy for his boots","My mama used to tell me stories about a place called Heaven","A story? The day I met my crew... I was starving, sitting on a curb, shaking"},false,false,{[1]={{t="Looked like brass, so I took it to a pawnshop. Man tapped the little bowler and said it was painted plastic",afterMs=2600},{t="I told him I'd won it. Hell knows why, because then he asked what league I bowled in",afterMs=2800},{t="Couldn't name one. Kept the damn thing on the floor of the car for weeks afterward",afterMs=3000}},[2]={{t="Sunday collection plate, easy as pie, he wept like a baby",afterMs=2600},{t="Funny thing is, I felt nothing, and that scared me more than the shaking",afterMs=2800},{t="Then the dead came, and suddenly I wasn't the scariest thing around",afterMs=3000}},[3]={{t="Boss screamed at me every day for six years, six damn years",afterMs=2600},{t="Day it all fell apart, I walked into his office, and he was already... gone",afterMs=2800},{t="I took his chair, his keys, and his gun, best promotion I ever got",afterMs=3000}},[4]={{t="He saved me from three dead guys in the alley on day two",afterMs=2600},{t="Took a bite that was meant for me, I held him until he stopped",afterMs=2800},{t="Haven't cried since, but I think about that dog every single night",afterMs=3000}},[5]={{t="Took four of us to carry it, we dropped it on the interstate, played it all night",afterMs=2600},{t="Wasn't even a good song, honestly, but we laughed so hard we cried",afterMs=2800},{t="Wish I could go back there for one night, just one",afterMs=3000}},[6]={{t="Nice ones, steel toes, perfect fit, he cried about it",afterMs=2600},{t="Found out later he was a vet who'd lost his legs, boots were for his brother",afterMs=2800},{t="I kept the boots, but I still dream about his face, funny how that works",afterMs=3000}},[7]={{t="I said, mama, if there's a Heaven, I'm not on the list",afterMs=2600},{t="She said, baby, everybody's on the list, they just have to knock",afterMs=2800},{t="I don't know about knocking, but I sure as hell am knocking now",afterMs=3000}},[8]={{t="A big guy named Dutch tossed me a can of peaches, didn't say a word",afterMs=2600},{t="I ate it all in one go, cried, and followed him for three days",afterMs=2800},{t="That's the nicest thing anyone's ever done for me, and he's dead now",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=law|st=neutral,careful",{"I answered a call about a blocked driveway outside Shepherdsville. Must've gone up and down that road twice","A story, huh? I once talked a man off a bridge in Louisville","First week on the force, I pulled over a lady for speeding, she was nine months pregnant"},false,false,{[1]={{t="Finally I found the house number and knocked. Woman came out in a hairnet, mad before I said a word",afterMs=2600},{t="I asked where the car was. She asked why I was at her back door on a Sunday morning",afterMs=2800},{t="Right house number, wrong road. I backed across that whole yard apologizing, and she followed me to the car",afterMs=3000}},[2]={{t="Three hours, freezing rain, he just wanted somebody to ask how his day was",afterMs=2600},{t="I asked, he told me, we both cried, and he climbed back over",afterMs=2800},{t="Haven't heard from him since this started, I hope he made it",afterMs=3000}},[3]={{t="Delivered the baby on the shoulder of I-65, in the rain, in my uniform",afterMs=2600},{t="They named him after me, little Calvin, I get a Christmas card every year",afterMs=2800},{t="This year I'm praying to get one",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=military|st=neutral,careful",{"At Knox, a corporal I knew wrote his whole name inside each sock. Right under the heel","My first day of basic, a drill sergeant stuck his nose an inch from mine and screamed for ten minutes","Army story? I was in the Gulf, carried a buddy half a mile across the sand"},false,false,{[1]={{t="Then the laundry mixed up two barracks. He was the only man who got all his own socks back",afterMs=2600},{t="Next evening there were half a dozen men bent over their socks, asking whether anybody had a laundry marker",afterMs=2800},{t="I used a ballpoint. Got a blue mark on each heel the first time I sweated",afterMs=3000}},[2]={{t="I didn't hear a word, all I could think was my mother's meatloaf",afterMs=2600},{t="He asked, what are you smiling at, private? and I said, meatloaf, sergeant",afterMs=2800},{t="Made me do push-ups till I cried, but he slipped me a candy bar that night",afterMs=3000}},[3]={{t="He weighed nothing, nothing at all, dehydrated to a rail",afterMs=2600},{t="He lived, got a medal, I got a bad knee and a letter",afterMs=2800},{t="That's one I'll keep until I'm gone",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=soldier_green|st=neutral,careful",{"Before I signed up, I bagged groceries in Muldraugh after school. They let me use the loudspeaker once","Um, a story? I don't have any, I'm nineteen, I just left home last month"},false,false,{[1]={{t="A woman had left her purse. I was supposed to call her up front, but I started reading her shopping list",afterMs=2600},{t="It was the first paper I pulled out. I got as far as baking powder before the manager stopped me",afterMs=2800},{t="She was only two aisles over. Came up and said she'd forgotten the baking powder",afterMs=3000}},[2]={{t="My mom packed me a lunch, the whole bus ride, I ate it on day one",afterMs=2600},{t="Now I'd give anything for a sandwich cut diagonally, the way she did",afterMs=2800},{t="Is that a story? I don't know, it's all I have",afterMs=3000}}}},
