{"TELL_STORY","reg=civilian,family,worker,rescue|tmp=fresh|st=friendly,neutral",{"A lady on our street kept a tortoise named Gerald, took him for a walk every day, I'd watch from my window","My dad taught me to drive in an empty church parking lot, and I hit the only tree","The week before ALL this -- I was complaining my boss never listened, and now I'd give anything to be yelled at by him","I once got stuck in a revolving door for twenty minutes, in front of my whole office","M-my grandmother kept a jar of buttons -- and every time I came over she let me pick one","We had a goat once that ate a whole pie, and the whole church watched","My sister and I used to race to the mailbox every day, and she always won, and I always let her","I had a pet turtle that escaped, and we found it in the garage three years later, ALIVE","The summer I turned twelve, I swam across the lake on a dare, and nobody believed me","My neighbor had a rooster that crowed at all the wrong times, I'd give a lot to hear that rooster right now"},false,false,{[1]={{t="Gerald was in front",afterMs=3200},{t="I think about that",afterMs=2500}},[2]={{t="The only tree in the whole lot",afterMs=3000}},[4]={{t="Best day of my life, compared to this",afterMs=3500}},[5]={{t="I've got one in my pocket right NOW!",afterMs=3000}},[6]={{t="The goat was fine, the pie wasn't",afterMs=3000}},[8]={{t="That's the only good story I have",afterMs=3500}},[9]={{t="Now I wish I'd stayed on the shore",afterMs=3500}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=civilian,family,worker,rescue|tmp=seasoned|st=friendly,neutral",{"I used to hunt with my father, and he'd say, a man who waits is a man who eats, I think about that a lot...","One winter the whole town got snowed in, forty people at the firehouse, one guitar, nobody left till spring","I knew a man who could fix any engine by listening, he'd put his ear to it like a doctor","Back in '82... the river rose, and we all piled on the roof, and the preacher sang hymns for three hours","An old man walked to town every day for sixty years, and when his legs gave out the town carried him","I once saw a deer walk right into a diner, order nothing, and walk out","My mother canned peaches every August, forty jars, and we ate the last one at her funeral","Years ago... I saved a kid from drowning, and I never found out his name, and I think about him","I worked a night shift once where nothing happened for eight hours, it was the best night of my life","The first time I saw the dead walk, I thought it was a parade, and I waved"},false,false,{[3]={{t="He's gone now, but I still listen to engines",afterMs=3500}},[6]={{t="Best customer we ever had",afterMs=3500}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=civilian,family,worker,rescue|st=friendly",{"The winter my daddy lost the farm, he sold the cows on a Tuesday and sat in the barn until dark","You want a story? Alright. My grandpa taught me to whistle by tying a string around my loose tooth","Asked my wife to marry me with a mouthful of fries, she laughed and said yes","Oh, I've got hundreds, but this one's my favorite, it's about my husband and a very angry goose","Alright, I'll tell you one, once I had a dog named Rufus, a mutt, ugly as sin","So my dad was a truck driver, gone for weeks","I'll tell you about the summer I fell in love","Let me tell you about my grandmother"},false,false,{[1]={{t="Mama brought him a plate and he said he wasn't hungry, which he'd never said in his life",afterMs=4500},{t="I was eleven. That's when I learned a man can sit perfectly still and be coming apart",afterMs=5000}},[2]={{t="Pulled it on the second try, and I whistled right through the hole it left, and he laughed so hard he had to sit down",afterMs=4500},{t="Last good tooth in the front of my head, and the best afternoon I ever had with him, so I call it even",afterMs=5000}},[5]={{t="He followed me home from school every day for six years",afterMs=3500},{t="I buried him under the apple tree, and I still talk to him",afterMs=4000}},[6]={{t="He'd call from payphones, always from a different state",afterMs=3500},{t="I kept all the postcards, they're in my backpack, right now",afterMs=4000}},[7]={{t="She worked at the Dairy Queen, we spent every night at the lake",afterMs=3500},{t="She moved away in August, I never saw her again, but I think about her",afterMs=4000}},[8]={{t="She could sew anything, fix anything, grow anything",afterMs=3500},{t="She'd say 'God doesn't give you more than you can handle', and I'd say 'then He's overestimating me'",afterMs=4000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=civilian,family,worker,rescue|st=careful",{"I don't tell stories to strangers!","Stories? now? you're kidding","No, and no","I don't have any stories for you","Stories are for friends, and you're NOT one yet!!","Not for you","My story's short, I trusted a stranger once this month - now I don't"}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=rescue_clergy|st=friendly,neutral",{"Mrs Hayes gave us her last loaf, next day we found her son alive, she wouldn't stop hugging him","A boy once climbed into the baptismal font during a service","My first funeral, the casket wouldn't fit through the door","There was a bell that rang every Easter for a hundred years"},false,false,{[2]={{t="and wouldn't get out",afterMs=3500},{t="the congregation sang louder",afterMs=3000}},[3]={{t="we had to tip it",afterMs=3500},{t="the widow laughed, and I've never forgotten that laugh",afterMs=3000}},[4]={{t="the year I was ordained, it cracked",afterMs=3200}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=militia|st=friendly,neutral",{"I could tell you a war story, but you wouldn't believe it, and I wouldn't tell it right","Shot a deer once at three hundred yards","When I was a boy, I got lost in a cornfield for six hours","We had a dog named Sarge"},false,false,{[2]={{t="my dad wept with pride",afterMs=3500},{t="I felt sick",afterMs=3000}},[3]={{t="my mother nearly skinned me",afterMs=3200}},[4]={{t="he outranked everyone",afterMs=3500}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=rescue_medical|st=friendly,neutral",{"A baby was born in the back of an ambulance on the night of the blackout, and I held her first, she cried, and I cried"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=civilian,family,worker,rescue|st=friendly,neutral|mood=funny",{"My uncle Dewey- he bet a man he could eat a whole pie in one sitting","Hah! one time, I locked myself out in my bathrobe, in front of the whole church picnic","My boy once glued a quarter to the sidewalk and watched people try to pick it up for an hour","There was this goat, see, at the county fair, and it ate the judge's hat","My wife made me a sandwich with the mayo on the outside, and I ate the whole thing","I once got chased by a goose for four blocks... ha","Old man Pruitt, he used to talk to his tomatoes, called them by name","Back in high school I got stuck in a locker, in front of the whole cafeteria","A fella in my town stole a church bell, once, as a joke!","My dog ate my homework, for real, and I got an A for creativity"},false,false,{[1]={{t="the pie was a mincemeat pie, ha",afterMs=3000},{t="he won, and we never spoke about what happened after",afterMs=2800}},[2]={{t="Reverend Tate brought me a tablecloth",afterMs=3200},{t="I wore it like a toga, best-dressed lady there",afterMs=2500}},[3]={{t="I should've been mad, but, ha, I laughed till I cried",afterMs=3000}},[4]={{t="the judge gave it first prize, ha",afterMs=3000},{t="the hat was a rental",afterMs=2500}},[5]={{t="I didn't have the heart to tell her",afterMs=3000},{t="she's gone now, and I'd eat that sandwich every day",afterMs=2800}},[6]={{t="a GOOSE",afterMs=2800},{t="I've been chased by worse since, but the goose still wins for sheer embarrassment",afterMs=2500}},[7]={{t="best tomatoes in the county",afterMs=3200},{t="his wife said it was the fertilizer, he said it was the manners",afterMs=2800}},[8]={{t="they cheered",afterMs=3000},{t="it was the high point of my social career",afterMs=2200}},[9]={{t="it took six men to put it back",afterMs=3200},{t="nobody ever found out it was the preacher's own brother",afterMs=2500}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=civilian,family,worker,rescue|st=friendly,neutral|mood=warm",{"There was a woman in the line at the grocery, years ago, who paid for my milk when I came up short","A stranger fixed my flat on a rainy night and wouldn't take a dime!","My neighbor brought a pot of soup the day my husband died, didn't say a word, just set it on the porch","The week the power went out in '88, the whole block grilled everything in their freezers","My daddy used to whistle when he walked in the door, always the same tune","Me and my brother got lost in the woods once, and our dog led us home","An old man gave me his seat on the bus, when I was pregnant and miserable","The preacher at our church always saved me the last cookie, because I was the only kid who said thank you!"},false,false,{[1]={{t="I never got her name",afterMs=3500},{t="I've been paying it forward ever since",afterMs=3000}},[2]={{t="he said, \"somebody'll do it for your daughter one day\"",afterMs=3200},{t="I think about that more than you'd guess",afterMs=3000}},[3]={{t="I ate it standing in the kitchen and bawled",afterMs=3500}},[4]={{t="best week of my life, forty people, a thousand hot dogs",afterMs=3200}},[5]={{t="I whistle it now, when I'm scared, and it helps!!",afterMs=3500}},[6]={{t="that dog's been dead twenty years, and I still thank him",afterMs=3000}},[7]={{t="he was seventy, and he stood the whole ride",afterMs=3000},{t="I cried at the next stop",afterMs=2500}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=civilian,family,worker,rescue|st=friendly,neutral|mood=sad",{"I still set out two plates","Last thing my husband said to me was \"we're out of milk\"","My dad's boots are still by the door","I found a note on the fridge, in my mother's handwriting","My daughter's last drawing was a horse, purple, with wings","I buried my brother with his watch on...","We were going to put a deck on the back this summer...","M-my wife's reading glasses are in my shirt pocket","The dog keeps waiting on the porch for the school bus","I didn't cry when it happened"},false,false,{[1]={{t="then I put one back",afterMs=3500},{t="every night I put one back",afterMs=3000}},[2]={{t="that's all I got",afterMs=3500},{t="I keep buying milk",afterMs=3000}},[3]={{t="size thirteen",afterMs=3200},{t="nobody in this house can wear them",afterMs=2800}},[4]={{t="\"Gone to find you\"",afterMs=3200},{t="I was out looking for her",afterMs=3500}},[5]={{t="I carry it, folded, in my coat",afterMs=3500},{t="the horse is wrinkled, now",afterMs=3000}},[6]={{t="it's still ticking, probably",afterMs=3500},{t="I think about that watch more than I should",afterMs=3000}},[7]={{t="I'd already bought the lumber",afterMs=3200},{t="it's still sitting in the yard, getting rained on",afterMs=3000}},[8]={{t="she was always losing them, so I'd carry them",afterMs=3200},{t="habit... I guess..",afterMs=3000}},[9]={{t="bus ain't come since the sixth",afterMs=3500}},[10]={{t="I cried three days later over a can opener",afterMs=3000},{t="sat in the kitchen and bawled over a can opener",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=civilian,family,worker,rescue|st=friendly,neutral|mood=grim",{"First time I saw one, I thought it was a drunk, so I walked up and asked if he needed help","I was in a grocery store when it started... and a man bit a lady in the cereal aisle","There was a night we hid in a cellar, nine of us, and one of them started pounding on the door","I watched a church burn once, with the doors chained from outside","My neighbor turned on a Thursday","We saw a man trying to climb a fence, with one of them right behind","I killed my first one with a garden hoe"},false,false,{[1]={{t="he turned around",afterMs=3500},{t="I ran so fast I lost a shoe",afterMs=3000}},[2]={{t="I walked out, left my cart",afterMs=3500},{t="still think about the cart",afterMs=3000}},[3]={{t="it pounded all night",afterMs=3500},{t="at dawn it stopped, and nobody said a word for an hour",afterMs=3200}},[4]={{t="nobody has ever said who did it",afterMs=3500},{t="I haven't been to church since",afterMs=3000}},[5]={{t="I could hear it through the wall",afterMs=3500},{t="I put on the TV loud so my kids wouldn't hear",afterMs=3000}},[6]={{t="we didn't help",afterMs=3500},{t="that one I carry",afterMs=3000}},[7]={{t="I washed that hoe for an hour",afterMs=3500},{t="it's in the garden shed, I won't use it again",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=civilian,family,worker,rescue|st=friendly,neutral|mood=calm",{"I was born in the back of a station wagon, in the parking lot of the county hospital..","The summer I turned ten -- I caught a catfish bigger than my leg","We used to have a barn dance every October, fiddles, jugs, cider","One winter, we had a snow so deep the school closed for a week","My grandmother could shell peas faster than a machine","I worked a summer on a tobacco farm, hanging leaves in the barn","The first time I saw the Ohio River, I was six, and I thought it was the ocean","My daddy drove a milk truck, and every morning at four he'd honk twice outside, so my mother knew he was coming"},false,false,{[1]={{t="my mother never let me forget it",afterMs=3000},{t="I never owned a station wagon",afterMs=2800}},[2]={{t="my granddad took a picture",afterMs=3200},{t="it's the only photo I still have of him",afterMs=3000}},[3]={{t="I met my husband at one, he stepped on my foot",afterMs=3200},{t="thirty-one years, and he never learned to dance",afterMs=2800}},[4]={{t="best week of my childhood",afterMs=3200},{t="we built a fort the size of a house",afterMs=2800}},[5]={{t="she'd talk the whole time, never looked down",afterMs=3200},{t="I can still hear it",afterMs=3000}},[6]={{t="the smell never leaves",afterMs=3000},{t="I still smell it sometimes, in my sleep",afterMs=2800}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=civilian,family,worker,rescue|tmp=fresh|st=friendly,neutral|mood=fear",{"I hid in a bathtub for two days, behind a shower curtain, with a butcher knife","We were in the car, and the road was blocked, and they were all around!","I heard my mother screaming from the next room, and I just- stayed","I got stuck on a roof once, for hours, with the dead below!"},false,false,{[1]={{t="I never used it",afterMs=3500},{t="but I held it so tight my hand cramped for a week",afterMs=3000}},[2]={{t="my husband said \"drive\"",afterMs=3500},{t="and I did, and I don't remember anything after that",afterMs=3000}},[3]={{t="I stayed",afterMs=3500},{t="I can't tell that story... I'm sorry, I thought I could",afterMs=3000}},[4]={{t="I counted them",afterMs=3500},{t="fifty-two",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=civilian,family,worker,rescue|tmp=seasoned|st=friendly,neutral|mood=funny",{"Back when I was a rookie, I forgot my lunch pail on the roof, and flew it off the side","I once sold a man a lawnmower, with a bag of fertilizer, and a hat, and a gallon of gas","There's a man in my town who has parked in the same spot every day for thirty years"},false,false,{[1]={{t="it landed on the foreman's truck",afterMs=3200},{t="he never found out it was mine",afterMs=2800}},[2]={{t="he came in for a nail",afterMs=3500}},[3]={{t="the day before this started, someone took his spot",afterMs=3200},{t="he was furious",afterMs=2800},{t="of all the things",afterMs=2500}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=civilian,family,worker,rescue|st=friendly|mood=warm",{"You're a good listener, you know that? I haven't told that story to anyone in years","Best Christmas of my life, we had no decorations, no money and a ham somebody left on our step"},false,false,{[1]={{t="it's about my wife and a bad pot roast",afterMs=3200},{t="she'd have liked you",afterMs=2800}},[2]={{t="Mama cried, Daddy laughed, and we ate it standing up in our coats because the wood was wet and the house was cold",afterMs=4800},{t="Nobody ever found out whose ham it was. We still say grace over it every year",afterMs=5000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=civilian,family,worker,rescue|st=friendly,neutral|day=0,99999|fact=recent_zombie_contact",{"N-not now, not now, I'll tell you when they've gone!","A story? with that outside? you're joking","Later... and I'll make it a good one!","I can't focus, I can't think, I'm sorry","Ask me when it's safe, I'll tell you everything"}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=civilian_loner|st=friendly,neutral",{"Once, I tracked a buck for three days","I fell through ice at the pond when I was twelve","My granddad taught me to read a trail","I saw a bear once, standing on its hind legs, like a man"},false,false,{[1]={{t="ended up face to face",afterMs=3500},{t="we both stood there",afterMs=3000},{t="then I let him go",afterMs=2800}},[2]={{t="my dog pulled me out",afterMs=3500},{t="best dog I ever had",afterMs=3000}},[3]={{t="before he taught me to read a book",afterMs=3500},{t="I think I got the better end",afterMs=3000}},[4]={{t="it looked at me",afterMs=3500},{t="I looked at it",afterMs=3000},{t="we agreed to go different ways",afterMs=2800}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=civilian_loner|st=careful",{"No stories"}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=family_elder|st=friendly,neutral",{"I was seventeen when I met my husband, at a square dance","In '55 the creek flooded and we canoed to church","When I was a girl... we ran a dairy","Married at seventeen, raised four kids, sixty-one years in the same house - ain't much more to tell"},false,false,{[1]={{t="he stepped on my foot",afterMs=3500},{t="forty-nine years later, he stepped on it again",afterMs=3000}},[2]={{t="the preacher gave the whole sermon wet to the knees",afterMs=3500}},[3]={{t="I milked at four",afterMs=3200},{t="I still wake at four",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=family_elder|st=careful",{"Not today"}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=family_youth|st=friendly,neutral",{"One time I got locked in the school bathroom overnight","Me and my friends drove to Louisville once, without telling anyone"},false,false,{[1]={{t="it was horrifying",afterMs=3500},{t="and kind of the best night of my life",afterMs=3000}},[2]={{t="we got a flat tire",afterMs=3500},{t="we walked home",afterMs=3000},{t="my mom grounded me for a month",afterMs=2800}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=worker|st=friendly,neutral",{"I once repaired a combine in a thunderstorm","We had a foreman who never said a word","I fell off a ladder once... into a barrel of sawdust"},false,false,{[1]={{t="with a coat hanger and a prayer",afterMs=3500},{t="it ran for ten more years",afterMs=3000}},[2]={{t="for twenty years",afterMs=3500},{t="he cried at my retirement party",afterMs=3000}},[3]={{t="came up laughing",afterMs=3200},{t="nobody else did",afterMs=2800}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=family_man,family_woman|st=friendly,neutral",{"The day my daughter was born... I got lost driving to the hospital","My son took his first steps toward a cat","Last Christmas we put the tree up in July by mistake.."},false,false,{[1]={{t="I'd driven that road a thousand times",afterMs=3500},{t="I was crying too hard to see",afterMs=3000}},[2]={{t="the cat ran",afterMs=3200},{t="he ran after it",afterMs=2800},{t="he hasn't stopped",afterMs=3000}},[3]={{t="the kids thought it was hilarious",afterMs=3500},{t="and now I wish we'd kept it up",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=rescue_firefighter|st=friendly,neutral",{"I once pulled a cat from a tree, and the cat bit me","My first fire, I forgot to turn off my radio","We rescued a goat from a well once"},false,false,{[1]={{t="the owner thanked the cat",afterMs=3500}},[2]={{t="the chief heard me praying out loud",afterMs=3200}},[3]={{t="the goat wouldn't leave",afterMs=3500},{t="we named her Betty",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=raider|st=hostile",{"You want a story? Here's one: a guy asked me too many questions, and now he's feeding the crows","Story time's over, friend, I'm tired of talking, and you're about to be tired of breathing"},false,false,{[1]={{t="The end",afterMs=2400}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=raider|st=friendly",{"A real one, huh... first night, I hid in a bathtub for eleven hours, listening to my neighbors die"},false,false,{[1]={{t="Eleven hours, {g:man|lady}, every scream I can still hear",afterMs=2600},{t="When I finally climbed out, the sun was up and it was so quiet, so wrong",afterMs=2800},{t="I haven't been the same since, I don't think I ever will be",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=gang|st=neutral,careful",{"Story? A'ight... my uncle ran numbers on Broadway for thirty years","So, the first night, my whole crew was at a cookout, music loud, everybody laughing","A story, huh... my mama raised me on Sundays, gospel and fried chicken","Yo, you want to hear something crazy? I got shot once, in the leg, over a pair of sneakers"},false,false,{[1]={{t="Never carried a gun, never raised his voice, everybody loved him",afterMs=2600},{t="Day it all fell apart, he stood on the corner and handed out groceries",afterMs=2800},{t="They got him anyway, but he went smiling, hand to God",afterMs=3000}},[2]={{t="Then somebody's uncle starts walking funny, bites a girl on the neck",afterMs=2600},{t="We ran, scattered like roaches, six of us made it out of twenty-two",afterMs=2800},{t="I still hear that music in my head, I can't shake it",afterMs=3000}},[3]={{t="I left at fifteen, thought I knew better, found the block, found my brothers",afterMs=2600},{t="Never thought I'd miss her cooking more than I miss my own freedom",afterMs=2800},{t="If I find her alive, I'm going to church, I'm going to church every day",afterMs=3000}},[4]={{t="Pair of white sneakers, brand new, I'd saved for two months",afterMs=2600},{t="Guy laughed at me, I laughed back, he shot, I walked it off",afterMs=2800},{t="Funny thing is, now I'd trade the whole world for an hour in those sneakers",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=gang|st=hostile",{"Story? I don't tell stories to cops, snitches, or strangers, which one are you?"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=gang|st=friendly",{"Alright, quick one, I had a little sister who sang in the choir"},false,false,{[1]={{t="Voice like an angel, no lie, people stopped on the street",afterMs=2600},{t="Day it started, she was at rehearsal, I haven't seen her since",afterMs=2800},{t="I still hum her songs, when nobody's around, I hum them",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=club|st=neutral,careful",{"A story, huh? Buried my best friend in a cornfield outside Elizabethtown","I've got one... the club threw a funeral for an old brother, big turnout, sixty bikes","Back in '71, I rode from Louisville to Daytona on a stolen bike and a bad attitude"},false,false,{[1]={{t="Name was Hank, we rode together twenty-two years, never missed a rally",afterMs=2600},{t="Day it got him, he stopped to help a woman on the side of the road",afterMs=2800},{t="I put the last round in him myself, and I'd do it again, God help me",afterMs=3000}},[2]={{t="Right in the middle of the eulogy, the dead guy sits up in the casket",afterMs=2600},{t="Chaos, {g:brother|sister}, absolute chaos, we lost a dozen in ten minutes",afterMs=2800},{t="Now when I hear a eulogy I check the exits first",afterMs=3000}},[3]={{t="Slept in ditches, ate gas station hot dogs, fell in love with a waitress in Georgia",afterMs=2600},{t="Never saw her again... never forgot her, though",afterMs=2800},{t="That's the one I tell when I'm sentimental, which is more and more lately",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=club|st=hostile",{"Tell you a story? Sure, once upon a time, a man asked too many questions, the end"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=club|st=friendly",{"One story, {g:brother|sister}... my daddy was a coal miner, black lung at fifty"},false,false,{[1]={{t="He told me the world's divided into people who work with their hands and people who take from them",afterMs=2600},{t="I took a third way, I joined the club, and I've been trying to figure out which one I am ever since",afterMs=2800}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=crime|st=neutral,careful",{"A story? Very well, I once brokered a truce between two families over a plate of spaghetti","I was a junior accountant at a firm in Lexington, bored out of my mind"},false,false,{[1]={{t="It lasted eleven days, which, in my line of work, is a record",afterMs=2600},{t="Everyone was happy, until someone's cousin brought up an old debt",afterMs=2800},{t="That was the last peaceful meal I had",afterMs=3000}},[2]={{t="One of the partners, a very polite man, offered me a better life",afterMs=2600},{t="I said yes, and I've been doing his sums for thirteen years",afterMs=2800},{t="Strange to think the end of the world is the first honest job I've had",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=crime|st=friendly",{"You want a real one? My father was a barber, honest as the day is long"},false,false,{[1]={{t="He cut hair for judges and thieves alike, same price for both",afterMs=2600},{t="He used to say, son, every man's the same under the cape",afterMs=2800},{t="I think about that when the dead walk past, they're all the same under the cape",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=prison|st=neutral,careful",{"A story... I don't have any good ones, they're all bad ones","A story... my first day inside I cried so hard they gave me an extra blanket"},false,false,{[1]={{t="Had this cellmate, Dewey, from Paducah, made flowers out of toilet paper",afterMs=2600},{t="Roses, daisies, even a sunflower, handed them out on Fridays",afterMs=2800},{t="I don't know if he's alive, but I hope somebody's giving him flowers",afterMs=3000}},[2]={{t="The guard, big guy named Burke, said, kid, it gets easier",afterMs=2600},{t="It didn't, but I never forgot he said it",afterMs=2800},{t="He turned on the third day, I had to... I can't talk about that",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=prison|st=hostile",{"I don't tell stories! Stories get you hurt! Stop asking me things!"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=prison|st=friendly",{"I'll tell you a good one, since you asked nicely... I kept a sparrow in my cell for a week"},false,false,{[1]={{t="Snuck bread crumbs, named him Charlie, he sat on my shoulder",afterMs=2600},{t="Then a guard found out, and... never mind, I just like remembering the good part",afterMs=2800}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=outlaw|st=neutral,careful",{"Story? There's a bear in the hills behind my place, old male, one ear torn off","I once hunted a buck for three days, followed his tracks through snow"},false,false,{[1]={{t="Fourteen years I've been watching him, never a problem between us",afterMs=2600},{t="Day the dead came through, he stood on his hind legs and roared at them",afterMs=2800},{t="God's honest truth, that bear's the only reason I'm still here",afterMs=3000}},[2]={{t="Finally had him in my sights, perfect shot, and I couldn't pull the trigger",afterMs=2600},{t="He looked right at me, calm as a church, then walked off",afterMs=2800},{t="I've thought about that deer more than most people I've known",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=outlaw|st=friendly",{"Alright, one: my granddad moonshined in a cave near Mammoth, thirty years, never got caught"},false,false,{[1]={{t="Only way they found out was when he died and left me the recipe in his will",afterMs=2600},{t="I never made a drop, but I keep the paper, it's all I've got of him",afterMs=2800}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=law|st=hostile",{"No stories, I'm working, keep your hands where I can see them"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=law|st=friendly",{"Okay, I'll tell you one... my partner Eddie, twenty years on patrol together"},false,false,{[1]={{t="He kept a thermos of terrible coffee, drank it black, swore it kept him alive",afterMs=2600},{t="Day he was bitten, he handed me the thermos and said, finish it",afterMs=2800},{t="I haven't been able to, it's still in my bag",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=law_sheriff|st=neutral,careful",{"When I took this badge, I swore I'd never fire my weapon in the line of duty"},false,false,{[1]={{t="Thirty-one years, I didn't, not once",afterMs=2600},{t="This week I've fired more rounds than all those years combined",afterMs=2800},{t="That's the kind of story I don't tell, but there it is",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=military|st=hostile",{"No stories, no questions, back away and do as you're told"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=military|st=friendly",{"Alright, one: my first night at Knox, I got lost looking for the mess hall"},false,false,{[1]={{t="Wandered for an hour, finally asked a janitor, he led me there",afterMs=2600},{t="Turned out he was the base commander in a work shirt, I almost died",afterMs=2800},{t="He laughed and gave me extra pie, that's the Army I miss",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=militia|st=neutral,careful",{"Story? Our barn burned down the summer I turned twelve","My granddad fought at Normandy, never talked about it"},false,false,{[1]={{t="Whole community came, brought lumber, built a new one in a weekend",afterMs=2600},{t="Forty families, working side by side, singing hymns",afterMs=2800},{t="That's what I'm defending now, not the land, the people on it",afterMs=3000}},[2]={{t="One Christmas he got drunk and told me everything, all night, in a whisper",afterMs=2600},{t="Said he only bleeds for neighbors who'd bleed for him",afterMs=2800},{t="I think about that every time I take watch",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=militia|st=friendly",{"I'll tell you a good one... we had a rooster named General, meanest bird you ever saw"},false,false,{[1]={{t="He chased the sheriff off our porch once, in front of the whole congregation",afterMs=2600},{t="Last week he crowed at dawn, loud as ever, the whole farm cheered",afterMs=2800},{t="Small things, friend, small things keep us going",afterMs=3000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=civilian,family,worker,rescue|st=neutral",{"A story? Maybe later, I'm not in the mood","Not now, I'd rather listen to yours"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=family|st=friendly",{"Gather round, child, I've got one about the winter of '58, when the river froze solid"},false,false,{[1]={{t="We skated to church, every Sunday, all of us",afterMs=3500},{t="I've never been so cold, or so happy",afterMs=4000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=law,swat|st=friendly",{"I'll tell you about my first week on the job"},false,false,{[1]={{t="A cat in a tree, a cow in the road, a drunk in a fountain",afterMs=3500},{t="I thought, 'this is easy', then the real calls came",afterMs=4000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=military,elite|st=friendly",{"I'll tell you about basic"},false,false,{[1]={{t="A drill sergeant named Hill, who could curse for ten minutes without repeating himself",afterMs=3500},{t="I miss him, I mean it, I miss that foul-mouthed bastard",afterMs=4000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=outlaw,raider,gang,club,crime,prison|st=friendly",{"I'll tell you about the time I robbed a church"},false,false,{[1]={{t="The pastor chased me with a Bible, I ran so fast I lost a shoe",afterMs=3500},{t="I still have the Bible, never opened, but I keep it",afterMs=4000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=outlaw,raider,gang,club,crime,prison|st=careful,hostile",{"Story? Here's one: once upon a time, you shut up"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=civilian,family|tmp=fresh|st=friendly,neutral|world=door",{"My sister and me swore we'd meet at the Riverside post office - I waited two days, then I found her writing on the door - 'waited two days'"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=civilian,family|role=family_woman,civilian_woman|tmp=fresh|st=friendly,neutral|world=vehicle",{"Last thing my husband said to me was pick up dog food on the way home - I picked it up, it's still in the trunk"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=civilian,family|tmp=fresh|st=friendly,neutral",{"There's a lady in {town} who still waters her flower beds every morning at seven - she waves - I wave, neither of us says a word"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=civilian,family|tmp=fresh|st=friendly,neutral|world=building",{"Found a birthday card in a mailbox on Saturday, to a boy named Kyle - ten dollars inside, I left it right there - it's his"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=civilian,family|role=family_man,family_woman,civilian_man,civilian_woman|tmp=fresh|st=friendly,neutral|hour=20,5|world=water",{"Fireworks over the river on the Fourth, my boy fell asleep on my shoulder before the finale - that was the last good night"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=civilian,family|role=family_man,family_woman,civilian_man,civilian_woman|tmp=fresh|st=friendly,neutral",{"A soldier at the roadblock gave my little girl his candy bar - he looked younger than my nephew, didn't say a word"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=civilian,family|tmp=fresh|st=friendly,neutral|world=road",{"My neighbor set his battery singing Santa out in the road to draw them off - it worked, they tore that Santa apart while we ran"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|st=friendly,neutral|world=road",{"Woman down my road rang her dinner bell at six every evening so her husband could find the house - rang it till it brought the wrong ones"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|st=friendly,neutral",{"Found a man up a deer stand past Ekron, rifle on his lap, dead of nothing I could see - crossword finished in pen - every square"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|st=friendly,neutral|world=trees,wind",{"Buried my neighbor under his own apple tree, next morning there was one apple sitting on the grave - probably the wind - probably"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|st=friendly,neutral|hour=20,5",{"The church bell in {town} rang at midnight three nights running, and there wasn't a soul in that church"},false,false,{[1]={{t="Third night I walked up there with a lantern and stood in the doorway. The rope was still swinging, slow, like somebody had just let go of it",afterMs=4500},{t="I didn't go in. Next morning I cut that rope down and burned it, and the bell hasn't rung since",afterMs=5000}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=civilian,family|tmp=fresh,seasoned|st=friendly,neutral",{"Met a man walking up 31W with a mattress on his back - said he'd leave the county, but not without his bed"},false,false,{[1]={{t="He'd carried it all the way from Muldraugh. By the Ekron turnoff he set it down, lay out flat on it, and told me he was done walking",afterMs=5000},{t="I left him my canteen. Came back that way next day and the mattress was still there, and the canteen was gone, and so was he",afterMs=5200}}}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=civilian,family,worker,rescue|st=hostile",{"Story time's over before it started - get"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=rescue|role=rescue_firefighter|st=friendly,neutral",{"Pulled an old woman out of a trailer fire on the tenth - she made me go back in for her canary, the bird outlived her by a week"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=rescue|role=rescue_medical|st=friendly,neutral",{"Man came into the ER with his ear in a sandwich bag - I asked if he'd press charges on his wife, he said no, she just wasn't herself"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=rescue|role=rescue_clergy|st=friendly,neutral|world=building",{"A couple asked me to marry them on the twelfth, in the church basement, by flashlight - I did, best wedding I ever did"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=worker|st=friendly,neutral",{"Quarry horn's on a timer, still goes off at five every day over an empty pit - and I still pick up my lunch pail when it does"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=law,swat|st=friendly,neutral",{"First call came in on the ninth, man biting a gas station clerk on 31W, I told dispatch it sounded like a normal Friday"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=law|st=friendly,neutral",{"Mr. Hensley called us every week about kids in his yard - last week I drove out - no kids, he just wanted somebody to come"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=law,swat|st=careful,hostile",{"I'm not here to tell stories - tell me yours - where'd you come from?"},false,{[1]="GENERIC"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=military|tmp=fresh|st=friendly,neutral",{"First night on the wire a man walked up holding a baby, begging, we couldn't let him through... that's my story"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=military,elite|tmp=seasoned,veteran|st=friendly,neutral",{"Had a private who said the same thing in his sleep every night - 'five more minutes, Mom.' Nobody woke him early after that"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=elite|st=friendly,neutral",{"Went in with eight, came out with eight, that's the only kind of story I tell"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=military,elite|st=careful,hostile",{"No stories on duty, move along"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=outlaw,crime|st=friendly,neutral",{"Stole a big white convertible in Louisville in '88, drove it home, and it was my own uncle's - he let me keep it - family's family","Cracked a safe in West Point last week, took all night, inside was a wedding album and a baby tooth - put it all back - don't tell nobody"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=raider,gang,club|st=friendly,neutral|world=vehicle",{"Fella begged us to take everything but his wedding ring - so we took the ring - hahaha, cried more over that than the truck"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=prison|st=friendly,neutral",{"Chased a guard the length of the yard the day it all went bad - then one of them chased him faster - Fair's fair"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=outlaw,raider,gang,club,crime,prison|st=careful",{"Stories are for friends, you ain't one yet"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=outlaw,raider,gang,club,crime,prison|st=hostile|world=road",{"Here's a story, nosy stranger, empty road, bang - the end"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=civilian|tmp=fresh|st=friendly,neutral",{"My story's nine days long and about four sentences - you want 'em or not?"},false,{[1]="GENERIC"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=worker|tmp=seasoned|st=friendly,neutral|world=vehicle",{"Hauled freight eighteen years, I can name every truck stop between here and Nashville"}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=rescue_clergy|st=neutral|mood=sad",{"I buried a man on the sixth whose name I never got - that's the story I keep telling"}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=law_sheriff|st=neutral|mood=funny|world=vehicle",{"I'll tell you one about a stolen tractor in 1979 - last funny thing that happened here"}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=soldier_nco|tmp=veteran|st=neutral",{"Everything worth telling happened somewhere I can't name, to somebody I can't name"}},
{"TELL_STORY","role=elite_delta|tmp=veteran|st=careful,neutral",{"No stories, stories are how folks find out where you've been"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=club|st=neutral|mood=funny",{"Which one? The one with the bridge, or the one my lawyer said not to tell?"},false,{[1]="GENERIC"}},
{"TELL_STORY","reg=raider,prison|tmp=predator|st=hostile",{"My story's short, everybody who told me no is gone and I'm still walking around"}},
